## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary: 14 findings — 8 Critical, 0 High, 2 Medium, 0 Low

This suite is the textbook **coverage-touching** anti-pattern. All 10 production methods are called (achieving ~95% line coverage), but **6 tests have zero assertions** and **4 more use only `Assert.IsNotNull`** — a trivially-satisfied check. These tests cannot catch regressions; every one would still pass if the production code returned garbage.

---

### ✅ Positive Observations

- Each test uses a fresh `InMemoryStore` via `[TestInitialize]` — good isolation, no shared state.
- No flakiness indicators (no `Thread.Sleep`, `DateTime.Now`, randomness).
- No swallowed exceptions or `try/catch` blocks.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic — entire file)

The suite methodically calls every public member of `ProductCatalog` in declaration order with no meaningful verification. This inflates coverage metrics while proving nothing about correctness.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — 6 tests (lines 17–21, 33–36, 39–43, 64–66, 69–74, 85–88)

These tests execute code and silently pass regardless of outcome:

| Test | Line | What's unverified |
|------|------|-------------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Product never read back to confirm it was saved |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 33 | Price never checked after update |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39 | Product never confirmed absent after removal |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 64 | Count value is discarded |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69 | Prices never checked after discount |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Imported products never verified |

**Example fix** — `AddProduct_Works`:
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 17-21)
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
```

**Example fix** — `UpdatePrice_Works`:
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 33-36)
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
```

**Example fix** — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`:
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 69-74)
